The `[profile]` layer can now be installed on a site built from the `volto` distribution. It creates its container with the portal type in `pas.plugins.identity.profile_container_type`, whose default is `Folder` — which that distribution does not allow at the portal root at all, so the install failed with a bare "Disallowed subobject type" naming neither the record to change nor the fact that a record exists. Volto is the frontend this package ships, so that was not an edge case to leave documented.

The configured type is still used wherever the parent allows it. Where it does not, `Document` is tried and then `Folder`, with a log line naming the record to set to silence it; a parent that allows neither raises an error naming the record and listing what it does allow. @ericof
